/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 48 0 R
/T (In a demand-paged system, a process runs with only some of its pages in main memory. When it references a page that is not in a frame, a page fault occurs. If every frame is full, the operating system must pick a victim page to replace. A reference to a page already in memory is a page hit. The quality of the replacement policy strongly affects performance, because each fault costs a disk access.)
/E (In a demand-paged system, a process runs with only some of its pages in main memory. When it references a page that is not in a frame, a page fault occurs. If every frame is full, the operating system must pick a victim page to replace. A reference to a page already in memory is a page hit. The quality of the replacement policy strongly affects performance, because each fault costs a disk access.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
