84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Optimal looks ahead in the reference string and evicts the page whose next use is farthest away, or which is never used again. It gives the minimum possible number of faults, but it cannot be built in a real OS because future references are unknown. It is used only as a benchmark. Tie rule used in this project: if several pages are never used again, the one that appears first in the frames is replaced.)
/E (Optimal looks ahead in the reference string and evicts the page whose next use is farthest away, or which is never used again. It gives the minimum possible number of faults, but it cannot be built in a real OS because future references are unknown. It is used only as a benchmark. Tie rule used in this project: if several pages are never used again, the one that appears first in the frames is replaced.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
