86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (FIFO keeps a queue of pages in the order they entered memory. When a fault occurs and no frame is free, the page at the front of the queue \(the oldest\) is replaced and the new page joins the back of the queue. It is simple and cheap, but it ignores how often or how recently a page is used, so a heavily used page can be evicted just because it was loaded early. FIFO also suffers from Belady's anomaly.)
/E (FIFO keeps a queue of pages in the order they entered memory. When a fault occurs and no frame is free, the page at the front of the queue \(the oldest\) is replaced and the new page joins the back of the queue. It is simple and cheap, but it ignores how often or how recently a page is used, so a heavily used page can be evicted just because it was loaded early. FIFO also suffers from Belady's anomaly.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
