88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (LRU assumes that the recent past predicts the near future. It records the time of last use of each page, on both hits and faults, and evicts the page with the oldest last-use time. It performs close to Optimal on programs with locality of reference, but a real system needs hardware support or extra bookkeeping to track recency.)
/E (LRU assumes that the recent past predicts the near future. It records the time of last use of each page, on both hits and faults, and evicts the page with the oldest last-use time. It performs close to Optimal on programs with locality of reference, but a real system needs hardware support or extra bookkeeping to track recency.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
