776 0 obj
<<
/Title (LRU better. At step 12, page 1 faults and all four frames are full. FIFO evicts page 4 because it is the oldest, yet page 4 is needed again at steps 13 and 15, so FIFO faults again on 4 and later on 3. LRU evicts page 5, which was last used at step 7 and is never needed again, so the later references to 2, 4 and 3 are all hits. Result: 8 faults for FIFO against 6 for LRU. FIFO equal. This string has only 5 distinct pages, so with 4 frames just one eviction is ever needed \(step 17, when page 4 first appears\). FIFO and LRU both evict page 5, so all three algorithms give the minimum of 5 faults. This case is a tie rather than a FIFO win, which the assignment allows \("better than or equal to"\). Overall, LRU beats FIFO when recently used pages are reused soon, and results depend on the access pattern.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 684 0 R
/Prev 833 0 R
>>
endobj
